<!--
  Two content pages in two languages. Each <url> carries xhtml:link
  alternates naming every language version of that page, including itself —
  Google requires the set to be reciprocal and self-referential.

  The site was nine pages until the Intro/Work/Art rebuild. Work is an
  outbound link to the LinkedIn profile, so it has no URL here. The retired
  pages are in _old/retired-pages/ and deliberately serve 404 — see
  CLAUDE.md, "The 2026 reduction".

  Deliberately excluded: /projects/ is a redirect stub carrying
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">, so listing it would ask
  Google to index a page that asks not to be indexed.

  No <lastmod>: on a hand-maintained sitemap the dates go stale immediately
  and a wrong date is worse than none.

  Regenerated by hand — `node validate.js` fails if this drifts from the
  pages that actually exist.
-->
